Implement Character #0001’s Basic Attack 2 (BA2) and Mid-Air Basic Attack 2 in the Alva repository.

Before editing anything, inspect the current main branch and understand the existing BA1 implementation. BA1 is already complete and merged; BA2 should extend the exact same architecture rather than creating a parallel combat/input system.

Terminology and naming

For these sprites:

* ba means basic attack
* 2ba means Basic Attack 2 / BA2
* The 2 before ba identifies which basic attack it is.
* The number at the very end of the filename is the animation frame number.

Examples:

* 0001_2ba1.png = Character #0001, Basic Attack 2, frame 1
* 0001_2ba7.png = Character #0001, Basic Attack 2, frame 7
* 0001_midair2ba1.png = Character #0001, Mid-Air Basic Attack 2, frame 1

BA2 is the secondary basic attack and belongs to the existing internal action2 input.

Do not rename the internal controller action from action2. Only change its player-facing label from Action 2 / A2 to Basic Attack 2 / BA2.

